---
description: Decide when a reused control should be a primitive or a library
alwaysApply: true
---

# UI primitives

When a control is used in more than one place, decide whether a shared
primitive is the better shape before copying it. Use a control from
`frontend/components/ui` when one already fits. Add a primitive there when
the same control will be reused. Do not restyle a one-off copy of a control
that already has a primitive.

For a large or specialized control, such as a chart, rich editor, or date
library, decide whether a small primitive is enough or a library is the
better fit. Ask before adding that dependency. Say what it is for, what it
costs to maintain, and what a smaller primitive would cover instead.

Choice lists use `Select` from `frontend/components/ui/select.tsx`. It opens
the themed list. Do not use a native `<select>` element. On Windows that
menu stays the browser's white list and ignores the app theme.

Date entry uses `DateField` from `frontend/components/ui/date-field.tsx`.
It opens the themed calendar. Do not use a native date input. On Windows
that calendar stays the browser's white widget and ignores the app theme.

Action menus stay `ActionMenu`. Text entry stays `Input`. A two-state setting uses `Switch` from `frontend/components/ui/switch.tsx`. Do not style a plain button to look like a label.
